# ─── companion-mac: the public/private seam ───
# The whitelabeled scaffolding (lib/, services/_template/, *.example, README,
# setup.sh) is PUBLIC. Anything you fill in to wire YOUR companion is PRIVATE
# and lives only here, never in git.

# Filled-in instance config
companion.conf
repos.conf
lib/boot-app/panes.conf
services/*/service.conf
services/*/.env

# Don't track the example-copied template instance, only the _template itself
services/_template/service.conf

# Generated boot-app + its source + snapshots
lib/boot-app/main.applescript
lib/boot-app/Companion-Boot.app/
lib/boot-app/Companion-Boot.app.bak.*

# Runtime state, logs, stdout
state/
*.log
*.stdout

# Any real service dir other than the template stays local until you choose to
# publish it. Uncomment to keep ALL instantiated services private by default:
# services/*
# !services/_template/
